                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ed4bb053-76ac-3372-9cfd-eaaf8fe25306",
                        "entry_id": "57a2120b-2380-3327-b1f0-6bb50df6421a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "маг, практикующий теургию"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f6262dc-e8d7-4c50-b224-c66af0b3eed5",
                                "sense_id": "ed4bb053-76ac-3372-9cfd-eaaf8fe25306",
                                "text": "В городах Малой Азии ― Никомидии, Пергаме, Смирне ― девятнадцатилетний Юлиан, искавший эллинской мудрости, слышал о знаменитом теурге и софисте, Ямвлике из Халкиды, ученике Порфирия неоплатоника, о божественном Ямвлике, как все его называли."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6a193d96-0e15-45f3-a5cf-b6e59a3a718c",
                        "source_entry_id": "57a2120b-2380-3327-b1f0-6bb50df6421a",
                        "source_sense_id": "ed4bb053-76ac-3372-9cfd-eaaf8fe25306",
                        "target_lang_word": "theurgist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "theurgist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0be8d16-7586-3a90-8425-a8c763847d49",
                                        "entry_id": "d61a9368-82b3-3a21-8e0f-15ea2e3030a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who claims or is alleged to perform magic with the aid of beneficent spirits."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe27713c-3861-4f12-a4a6-ed703b103687",
                        "source_entry_id": "57a2120b-2380-3327-b1f0-6bb50df6421a",
                        "source_sense_id": "ed4bb053-76ac-3372-9cfd-eaaf8fe25306",
                        "target_lang_word": "theurge",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "theurge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e1a040e-ad88-3032-8760-843d4217f950",
                                        "entry_id": "4ecf1c65-ec7b-3bb2-adcd-0c1382d4a5e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who works miracles, or persuades a god or spirit to perform a supernatural work."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3c17aad-2513-4201-b3f3-868f447a2715",
                                                "sense_id": "6e1a040e-ad88-3032-8760-843d4217f950",
                                                "text": "He acknowledged Christ to be a most excellent man, the friend of God, the admirable theurge; he denied, however, that Jesus designed to abolish entirely the worship of demons..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "937ef8c5-f77a-45b0-898a-bd2869836db8",
                                                "sense_id": "6e1a040e-ad88-3032-8760-843d4217f950",
                                                "text": "The father was known simply as a philosopher, the son as a theurge..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12b75dbb-703c-46ea-b5c2-531a15435bd7",
                                                "sense_id": "6e1a040e-ad88-3032-8760-843d4217f950",
                                                "text": "In other words, the theurge makes himself known to and recognized by the gods, like the mysta in his initiation, by means of 'symbols', signs or passwords (synthemata)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "272cb450-df93-468f-a9d6-0fdf20bb2841",
                                                "sense_id": "6e1a040e-ad88-3032-8760-843d4217f950",
                                                "text": "In this process the human mediator's own role was significantly increased from that of middleman theurge to god-imitating demiurge, not only bringing the images to life inside himself in the form of an “inner sculpting,” but...giving them external form as spirits as well."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
